<h1>Claude Sonnet 5 pricing: the September increase was cancelled</h1>
<p class="updated" style="color:#6B7689;font-size:14px;margin-top:-6px">Originally published 19 July 2026 · Updated 28 September 2026</p>
<div class="warning"><strong>Correction:</strong> Anthropic cancelled the planned September 1, 2026 price increase. Sonnet 5 did not move to $3/$15. Its standard public API rates remain $2 per million input tokens and $10 per million output tokens. The earlier deadline and price-rise analysis on this page has been removed because that scenario did not happen.</div>

<p>Anthropic's <a href="https://www.anthropic.com/news/claude-sonnet-5">Sonnet 5 launch announcement</a> was updated on August 10 to make the introductory $2/$10 price permanent. The current <a href="https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/about-claude/pricing">Claude API pricing documentation</a> lists the same rates. Any forecast that assumed a September increase should be corrected rather than carried forward as a cost event.</p>

<h2>Current Sonnet rates</h2>
<div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Model</th><th>Input per 1M tokens</th><th>Output per 1M tokens</th><th>Cache read</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td>Claude Sonnet 5</td><td>$2.00</td><td>$10.00</td><td>$0.20</td></tr>
<tr><td>Claude Sonnet 5.5</td><td>$2.00</td><td>$10.00</td><td>$0.20</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div>
<p>Anthropic's September 28 Sonnet 5.5 announcement lists the same base rates as Sonnet 5, plus $2.50 per million for 5-minute cache writes and $4.00 for 1-hour cache writes. Check the pricing page before procurement or production forecasts, since provider pricing can change.</p>

<h2>What Sonnet 5.5 changes for the cost model</h2>
<p>Sonnet 5.5 does not lower the published per-token price. Anthropic says the model generates output more than 30% faster and can cost up to 30% less per task for most work because it uses fewer tokens. Treat that as a launch claim and test it against your own workload. Faster output can reduce latency without reducing a token-metered bill; lower spend requires lower token use, fewer retries, or fewer escalations.</p>
<p>For each workload, track cost per accepted result, not just cost per request. Include input/output tokens, cache writes and reads, retries, tool calls, and any fallback to another model. Keep quality and human review rates in the comparison so a cheaper but less reliable run does not appear to be a saving.</p>

<h2>Recommended forecast update</h2>
<ol>
  <li>Remove the planned 50% Sonnet 5 rate increase from September and Q4 scenarios.</li>
  <li>Keep Sonnet 5.5 at the same per-token rate in the base case as Sonnet 5.</li>
  <li>Use a separate sensitivity case for reduced tokens per task; do not assume Anthropic's maximum 30% saving applies uniformly.</li>
  <li>Benchmark representative tasks and update the sensitivity with measured cost per accepted result.</li>
</ol>

<p>For launch details and an example task-cost model, read <a href="/research/sonnet-5-5-pricing-agent-cost-model">Sonnet 5.5 pricing: the $2/$10 rate and real task cost</a> and the <a href="/research/claude-sonnet-5-5-launch-and-model-routing">Sonnet 5.5 model-routing guide</a>.</p>
